Package: oneplus-erhai-otg
Version: 1.2
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: TheMojoMan <themojoman@gmx.net>
Description: ADSP OTG session re-arm for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai)
 On every USB-C detach the kernel driver erhai_otg_glink disarms the ADSP
 OTG session to keep the dwc3 island alive; on this ADSP firmware a
 disarmed session after a DP-altmode-capable partner leaves the Type-C CC
 attach detection dead (replugs are invisible until reboot). This package
 ships /usr/local/sbin/erhai-otg-rearm.sh, which re-arms the session over
 pmic_glink via the erhai_otg debugfs cmd knob (USB_OTG_AP_ENABLE=17,
 USB_OTG_SWITCH=18), a oneshot systemd unit, and a udev rule triggering it
 on Type-C port change / partner removal so every detach self-heals.
 Requires the erhai kernel (erhai_otg_glink + debugfs).
